{"step_index":17,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T22:35:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T04:05:31+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T04:05:33+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/3afa10cf-ab2f-45bb-8f37-5ccb114e7ae0/.system_generated/steps/10/content.md`\nTotal Lines: 489\nTotal Bytes: 18029\nShowing lines 300 to 489\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n300:         <li><strong>Topaz/TensorPix:</strong> High quality but paid ($299 or $30/hour)</li>\n301:         <li><strong>Free AI Video Upscaler:</strong> Works instantly in browser, no signup, no watermark, no limits, truly free forever</li>\n302:     </ul>\n303: \n304:     <p><strong>The secret:</strong> We use optimized AI models that run efficiently in your browser using WebGPU. Because your device does the work (not our servers), we can afford to let you upscale unlimited hours at zero cost to either of us.</p>\n305: \n306:     <h2>Step-by-Step Process</h2>\n307: \n308:     <h3>1. Upload Video</h3>\n309:     <ul>\n310:         <li>Drag and drop or click to select</li>\n311:         <li>Supports: MP4 and WebM files (any format your browser can play natively)</li>\n312:         <li>Need MKV, AVI, ProRes, or other formats? The <a href=\"https://fast.upscaler.video\">paid version</a> handles all video formats via server-side processing</li>\n313:         <li>No file size limits</li>\n314:     </ul>\n315: \n316:     <h3>2. Select Settings</h3>\n317:     <ul>\n318:         <li>Choose network size (small, medium, or large)</li>\n319:         <li>AI automatically enhances quality</li>\n320:     </ul>\n321: \n322:     <h3>3. Processing</h3>\n323:     <ul>\n324:         <li>Video processes on your device using your graphics card — integrated graphics (Intel HD, Apple M-series, AMD integrated) works fine. No dedicated GPU required.</li>\n325:         <li>Time varies based on: video length, resolution, your hardware</li>\n326:         <li>Typical: 2-5 minutes per minute of video</li>\n327:     </ul>\n328: \n329:     <h3>4. Download</h3>\n330:     <ul>\n331:         <li>Get your enhanced video</li>\n332:         <li>No watermark, no compression</li>\n333:         <li>Original quality preserved and enhanced</li>\n334:     </ul>\n335: \n336:     <h2>Requirements</h2>\n337: \n338:     <h3>Browser Compatibility</h3>\n339:     <p>Supports all major modern browsers with WebCodecs API (required for video processing):</p>\n340:     <ul>\n341:         <li><strong>Chrome 94+</strong> - WebGPU enabled by default (113+)</li>\n342:         <li><strong>Edge 94+</strong> - WebGPU enabled by default (113+)</li>\n343:         <li><strong>Opera 80+</strong> - WebGPU enabled by default (99+)</li>\n344:         <li><strong>Safari 16+</strong> - Uses WebGL fallback, Safari 26+ will have WebGPU enabled by default</li>\n345:         <li><strong>Firefox 130+</strong> - Uses WebGL fallback, <a href=\"/enable-webgpu\">WebGPU can be enabled</a></li>\n346:     </ul>\n347:     <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Note:</strong> Firefox and Safari currently use WebGL fallback for full compatibility. Quality is identical to WebGPU, processing is just 2-3x slower.</p>\n348: \n349:     <h3>Hardware</h3>\n350:     <ul>\n351:         <li>Any device with integrated or dedicated graphics — most modern laptops and desktops qualify. No dedicated GPU required.</li>\n352:         <li>Sufficient RAM (4GB+ recommended)</li>\n353:         <li>Stable internet for loading the page (processing happens offline)</li>\n354:     </ul>\n355: \n356:     <h2>Limitations</h2>\n357: \n358:     <h3>Processing Speed</h3>\n359:     <ul>\n360:         <li>Slower than server-based processing (uses your device, not our servers)</li>\n361:         <li>Typical: 2x-10x slower than paid server-side options</li>\n362:         <li>Trade-off: Free and unlimited vs. faster paid processing</li>\n363:     </ul>\n364: \n365:     <h3>Quality</h3>\n366:     <ul>\n367:         <li>Good quality enhancement using efficient models</li>\n368:         <li>For maximum quality, see our paid option: <a href=\"https://fast.upscaler.video\">fast.upscaler.video</a></li>\n369:     </ul>\n370: \n371:     <h3>Browser Requirements</h3>\n372:     <ul>\n373:         <li>Must keep browser tab open during processing</li>\n374:         <li>Large videos may take significant time</li>\n375:         <li>Mobile processing possible but slower</li>\n376:     </ul>\n377: \n378:     <h2>When to Use Free vs Paid</h2>\n379: \n380:     <h3>Use Free Version When:</h3>\n381:     <ul>\n382:         <li>Budget is a primary concern</li>\n383:         <li>Time is not critical</li>\n384:         <li>Processing occasional videos</li>\n385:         <li>Learning/experimenting with upscaling</li>\n386:         <li>File sizes under 1GB</li>\n387:     </ul>\n388: \n389:     <h3>Use Paid Version When:</h3>\n390:     <ul>\n391:         <li>Need results in minutes, not hours</li>\n392:         <li>You have a slower, or unsupported device</li>\n393:         <li>Require maximum quality</li>\n394:         <li>Working with very long files (more than 10 minutes)</li>\n395:         <li>Your video is in a format browsers can't play natively (MKV, AVI, ProRes, H.265, etc.) — the paid version handles all formats</li>\n396:         <li>Professional/commercial projects</li>\n397:     </ul>\n398: \n399:     <p>Paid version: $5 per hour of video processed<br>\n400:     <a href=\"https://fast.upscaler.video\">Learn more →</a></p>\n401: \n402:     <h2>Privacy & Security</h2>\n403: \n404:     <h3>Your Data</h3>\n405:     <ul>\n406:         <li>Videos never uploaded to our servers (free version)</li>\n407:         <li>Processing happens locally on your device</li>\n408:         <li>We don't store, view, or access your files</li>\n409:         <li>No account, no tracking of your videos</li>\n410:     </ul>\n411: \n412:     <h3>What We Collect</h3>\n413:     <ul>\n414:         <li>Anonymous usage statistics (page views, button clicks)</li>\n415:         <li>No personally identifiable information</li>\n416:         <li>No video content or metadata</li>\n417:     </ul>\n418: \n419:     <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>\n420: \n421:     <h3>\"WebGPU/WebGL Not Supported\" or \"WebCodecs Not Supported\"</h3>\n422:     <ul>\n423:         <li>Update your browser to the latest version (Chrome 94+, Edge 94+, Opera 80+, Safari 16+, Firefox 130+)</li>\n424:         <li>Try Chrome or Edge (best compatibility with WebGPU)</li>\n425:         <li>Firefox and Safari will automatically use WebGL fallback if available</li>\n426:         <li>Check if your GPU drivers are up to date</li>\n427:         <li><strong>Main limitation:</strong> WebCodecs API support (not available on older browsers or Firefox Android)</li>\n428:     </ul>\n429: \n430:     <h3>Processing Very Slow</h3>\n431:     <ul>\n432:         <li>Close other browser tabs</li>\n433:         <li>Close other applications</li>\n434:         <li>Check GPU usage in browser task manager</li>\n435:         <li>Consider paid version for faster processing</li>\n436:     </ul>\n437: \n438:     <h3>Browser Crashes</h3>\n439:     <ul>\n440:         <li>Video may be too large for your device</li>\n441:         <li>Try shorter video segments</li>\n442:         <li>Reduce target resolution</li>\n443:         <li>Use paid version for large files</li>\n444:     </ul>\n445: \n446:     <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n447: \n448:     <p><strong>Is it really free?</strong><br>\n449:     Yes, completely free. No trial, no credit card, no signup.</p>\n450: \n451:     <p><strong>What's the catch?</strong><br>\n452:     No catch. Processing uses your device, so we have no server costs. This is why we can offer unlimited free - we could theoretically let you upscale billions of hours and it would cost us $0.</p>\n453: \n454:     <p><strong>Will you add watermarks later?</strong><br>\n455:     No. Free version stays free and watermark-free.</p>\n456: \n457:     <p><strong>Can I use this commercially?</strong><br>\n458:     Yes, output videos are yours to use however you want.</p>\n459: \n460:     <p><strong>How do you make money?</strong><br>\n461:     We offer a <a href=\"https://fast.upscaler.video\">paid version</a> which implements AI Upscaling on professional GPU servers. Many users with longer, larger video files or older, slower devices would likely get better, faster results with the paid version</p>\n462: \n463:     <hr>\n464: \n465:     <p><a href=\"https://free.upscaler.video/\">← Back to Upscaler</a></p>\n466: \n467: </div>\n468: \n469: <footer style=\"background-color: #f9fafb; border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb; padding: 2rem 1rem; margin-top: 3rem; text-align: center; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #6b7280;\">\n470:     <div style=\"max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;\">\n471:         <div style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem;\">\n472:             <a href=\"https://free.upscaler.video/faq/\" style=\"color: #2563eb; margin: 0 0.75rem;\">FAQ</a>\n473:             <a href=\"https://free.upscaler.video/compare/\" style=\"color: #2563eb; margin: 0 0.75rem;\">Compare</a>\n474:             <a href=\"https://free.upscaler.video/how-it-works/\" style=\"color: #2563eb; margin: 0 0.75rem;\">How It Works</a>\n475:             <a href=\"https://free.upscaler.video/privacy/\" style=\"color: #2563eb; margin: 0 0.75rem;\">Privacy Policy</a>\n476:             <a href=\"https://free.upscaler.video/\" style=\"color: #2563eb; margin: 0 0.75rem;\">← Back to Upscaler</a>\n477:         </div>\n478:         <div>\n479:             Source code <a style=\"color: #2563eb;\" href=\"https://github.com/sb2702/free-ai-video-upscaler\">on Github</a>.\n480:             © Sam Bhattacharyya 2026\n481:         </div>\n482:     </div>\n483: </footer