tps://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/.gitignore)\n409: [LICENSE](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/LICENSE)\n410: [LICENSE](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/LICENSE)\n411: [README.md](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/README.md)\n412: [README.md](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/README.md)\n413: [package.json](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/package.json)\n414: [package.json](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/package.json)\n415: [tsconfig.json](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/tsconfig.json)\n416: [tsconfig.json](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/tsconfig.json)\n417: [webpack.demo.config.js](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/webpack.demo.config.js)\n418: [webpack.demo.config.js](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/webpack.demo.config.js)\n419: [webpack.prod.config.js](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/webpack.prod.config.js)\n420: [webpack.prod.config.js](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/webpack.prod.config.js)\n421: [yarn.lock](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/yarn.lock)\n422: [yarn.lock](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/yarn.lock)\n423: \n424: ## Repository files navigation\n425: - \n426: - [README](https://github.com/sb2702/websr)\n427: - [MIT license](https://github.com/sb2702/websr)\n428: [README](https://github.com/sb2702/websr)\n429: [MIT license](https://github.com/sb2702/websr)\n430: \n431: A free and open-source Javascript library / SDK for running practical, real-time AI Upscaling of videos and images on the web.\n432: [Check out the SDK in action in Free AI Video Upscaler!](https://free.upscaler.video/)\n433: Warning This project is very new and still in development, and shouldn't be used (yet) in production until stable. Expect API changes between versions and bugs\n434: \n435: - ✅ Real-time AI upscaling using WebGPU compute shaders\n436: - ✅ Multiple network sizes (Small, Medium, Large) for performance/quality tradeoffs\n437: - ✅ Pre-trained weights for Animation, Real Life, and 3D content\n438: - ✅ OffscreenCanvas support for worker thread processing\n439: - ✅ Custom training pipeline - train your own models\n440: - ✅ Manual render control for advanced use cases\n441: - ✅ Dynamic network switching at runtime\n442: \n443: ### Installation\n444: npm\n445: \n446: ```\n447: npm install @websr/websr\n448: ```\n449: \n450: yarn\n451: \n452: ```\n453: yarn add @websr/websr\n454: ```\n455: \n456: ### Quick Start\n457: ```\n458: import WebSR from '@websr/websr'; const video = document.getElementById('video'); // HTML Video Element const canvas = document.getElementById('canvas'); // Output canvas const gpu = await WebSR.initWebGPU(); if(!gpu) return console.log(\"Browser/device doesn't support WebGPU\"); const websr = new WebSR({ network_name: \"anime4k/cnn-2x-s\", weights: await (await fetch('./cnn-2x-s.json')).json(), //found in weights/anime4k folder gpu, canvas }); // Render loop using requestVideoFrameCallback function renderFrame() { websr.render(video).then(() => { video.requestVideoFrameCallback(renderFrame); }); } video.requestVideoFrameCallback(renderFrame);\n459: ```\n460: \n461: Note: Resolution is automatically detected from the source on first render. The canvas will be automatically resized to match the upscaled output (input resolution × network scale factor). If the source resolution changes, WebSR will automatically reinitialize with the new dimensions.\n462: \n463: ### OffscreenCanvas / Worker Thread\n464: WebSR is compatible with OffscreenCanvas, allowing you to run the upscaling in a worker thread to keep your main thread responsive:\n465: \n466: ```\n467: // main.js const canvas = document.getElementById('output'); const offscreen = canvas.transferControlToOffscreen(); const worker = new Worker('websr-worker.js'); const video = document.getElementById('video'); // Send canvas and video frames to worker worker.postMessage({ canvas: offscreen }, [offscreen]); // Use requestVideoFrameCallback to send frames to worker function sendFrame() { createImageBitmap(video).then(bitmap => { worker.postMessage({ frame: bitmap }, [bitmap]); video.requestVideoFrameCallback(sendFrame); }); } video.requestVideoFrameCallback(sendFrame);\n468: ```\n469: \n470: \n471: ```\n472: // websr-worker.js importScripts('./websr.js'); let websr; self.onmessage = async function(e) { if(e.data.canvas) { // Initialize WebSR in worker const gpu = await WebSR.initWebGPU(); websr = new WebSR({ network_name: \"anime4k/cnn-2x-s\", weights: await (await fetch('./cnn-2x-s.json')).json(), gpu, canvas: e.data.canvas }); } else if(e.data.frame && websr) { // Render frame await websr.render(e.data.frame); } };\n473: ```\n474: \n475: ### Network options\n476: There are currently 3 networks defined:anime4k/cnn-2x-s (small), anime4k/cnn-2x-m (medium) and anime4k/cnn-2x-l (large).\n477: \n478: ```\n479: anime4k/cnn-2x-s\n480: ```\n481: \n482: \n483: ```\n484: anime4k/cnn-2x-m\n485: ```\n486: \n487: \n488: ```\n489: anime4k/cnn-2x-l\n490: ```\n491: \n492: For each network, I've not only included with the weights from Anime4K, but I've also retrained the networks on Real Life and 3D (gaming/3d animation) content. These can be found in the [weights/anime4k folder](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/tree/main/weights/anime4k)\n493: For convenience, I've also included a [content detection style network](https://github.com/sb2702/websr/blob/main/weights/tflite/content_detection_mobilenet_v3.tflite) implemented in TFLite. You can use it as follows:\n494: \n495: ```\n496: import '@tensorflow/tfjs-backend-cpu'; import * as tf from '@tensorflow/tfjs-core'; import * as tflite from '@tensorflow/tfjs-tflite'; const contentDetectionCanvas = document.createElement('canvas'); contentDetectionCanvas.width = 224; contentDetectionCanvas.height = 224; const contentDetectionCtx = contentDetectionCanvas.getContext('2d', {willReadFrequently: true}); const tfliteModel = await tflite.loadTFLiteModel('./content_detection_mobilenet_v3.tflite', {} ); const source = //video, image, imageBitmap, etc... contentDetectionCtx.drawImage(source, source.width/2-112, source.height/2-112, 224, 224, 0, 0, 224, 224 ); // Take the center 224x224 crop of the source const input = tf.div(tf.expandDims(img), 255); const outputTensor = tfliteModel.predict(input); const values = outputTensor.dataSync(); if(values[1] > values[0]) //animation else: //real life // I tried building a 3-network classifier, but ran into some accracy issues\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
